{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi","id":339568,"title":"What are Arcanoi?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-13T17:07:17-08:00","id":339568,"title":"What are Arcanoi?","content":"So, I'm not terribly familiar with Wraith. I've taken a look at the core book, and I dig basically everything about it. I decided to pledge the Kickstarter and get in on this action.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the recent Stretch Goal update about including the Dark Kingdom of Jade Arcanoi (as well as the Arcanos previews on the KS page) raised a question in my mind.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not terribly familiar with Wraith, so I'm sorry if this is either entry-level information or an ultimately pointless question, but:<br /> <br /> Are Arcanoi socially-constructed phenomena? The previewed Arcanoi have both &quot;modern&quot; and &quot;ancient&quot; arts, implying that their usage has changed over time, even if they fall under the same themes. So, Argos is all about travel, regardless of what aspects of it you're mastering. And apparently the Arcanoi practiced in Stygia are different from those practiced in other Dark Kingdoms.<br /> <br /> So, what lies at the base of the Arcanoi? Are there any powers that are &quot;fundamental&quot; to Wraith-hood? Some Arcanoi, like Usury and Argos, seem like the sorts of things any ghost would find helpful in their day-to-day undeaths, so I'm having a hard time imagining how different other cultures' spooky magics might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T17:38:19-08:00","id":339588,"title":"","content":"If you are familiar with Vampire a rough comparaison would be Arcanoi is to wraith what Discipline is to vampire. It's a (gross) simplification but it's a good way to look at it.<br /> <br /> Like Disciplines they offert different power that varies with time...Look at the Discipline in Dark \u00c2ge, Victorian Era or Modern Night and some will varie quite a lot.<br /> <br /> Unlike Discipline though the Arcanoi are not Guild specific...sure the guilds will favor a specific Arcanoi but a wraith can mix and match them anyway it wants. Though stay clear of Dark and Forbidden Arcanoi, they can be bad news<br /> <br /> Again it's simplify...even grossly simplify in some cases, but it show help you get a better idea of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T19:01:51-08:00","id":339646,"title":"","content":"Well technically each Guild is connected to one of the sixteen main Arcanoi. You couldn't exactly be a member of the Harbinger Guild without Argos or a Pardoner without Castigate. Originally, those Guilds effectively controlled their particular Arcanoi within Stygia as they were the ones to really begin explore the nature of the Arcanoi and develop their power.<br /> <br /> There are several kinds of Arcanoi. There's the main Arcanoi which embody the common ghostly powers. In the western lands of the dead, within Stygia anyway, those sixteen powers were tied to the Guilds until they were broken several centuries ago, though the Guild do still exist albeit without much of the political power they possessed and still quite to their particular Arcanoi. The Arcanoi have become divided into four categories based on how useful they are to Stygian society and don't interfere with the world of the living. The Great Guilds and their Arcanoi are the most vital to Stygia and largely still operate openly. Beneath them are the Working Guilds whose powers are technically illegal but tolerated as they don't interfere with the Skinlands. Then there's the Criminal Guilds, their powers are illegal as they all affect the Skinlands and the living. Rounding them is the Forbidden Guilds which are pretty hated in addition to illegal.<br /> <br /> Of course that only applies to Stygia's official stance, not everyone within Stygia tows the party line and that doesn't extend to the Renegades and the Heretics.<br /> <br /> Then there are the other Dark Kingdoms. Many possess most or all of the common Arcanoi and some have their own unique Arcanoi as well, born out of the cultures and beliefs of those regions. To my knowledge those Arcanoi can only be learned by the wraiths of those Dark Kingdoms.<br /> <br /> Finally there are the Dark Acranoi of Spectres, though some are learned by Doomslayers, wraiths that explore the Labyrinth and fight the Spectres there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T19:47:55-08:00","id":339693,"title":"","content":"I don't know that there is any real basis for the arcanoi beyond simply being abilities wraiths can learn because they are wraiths. Most arts are fueled by pathos at least, though many require expenditure of willpower and can increase angst.<br /> <br /> Most arts replicate things that we generally think ghosts are capable of doing, much like disciplines replicate things we think of vampires of being able to do. <br /> <br /> It's suggested in the books occasionally that the underworld is <i>supposed</i> to be a place that guides the dead come to terms with their loss, and on to transcendence. However that function has become lost and corrupted, so instead of transcendence awaiting every wraith at the end, there instead is oblivion. (Transcendence is still possible, just more difficult, and the Hierarchy considers it a heresy.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, it could be that the Arcanoi were supposed to be tools for the wraith to use on their way to transcendence, a means to give their final farewells, etc. Perhaps the arcanoi are themselves corrupted as well, and expanded upon in ways they weren't meant to be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T21:00:10-08:00","id":339715,"title":"","content":"arcanoi are wraithly &quot;skills&quot; that at one time were given monopolies in the West. That's why they are called guilds after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T23:27:35-08:00","id":339774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi?p=339646#post339646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well technically each Guild is connected to one of the sixteen main Arcanoi. You couldn't exactly be a member of the Harbinger Guild without Argos or a Pardoner without Castigate. Originally, those Guilds effectively controlled their particular Arcanoi within Stygia as they were the ones to really begin explore the nature of the Arcanoi and develop their power.<br /> <br /> There are several kinds of Arcanoi. There's the main Arcanoi which embody the common ghostly powers. In the western lands of the dead, within Stygia anyway, those sixteen powers were tied to the Guilds until they were broken several centuries ago, though the Guild do still exist albeit without much of the political power they possessed and still quite to their particular Arcanoi. The Arcanoi have become divided into four categories based on how useful they are to Stygian society and don't interfere with the world of the living. The Great Guilds and their Arcanoi are the most vital to Stygia and largely still operate openly. Beneath them are the Working Guilds whose powers are technically illegal but tolerated as they don't interfere with the Skinlands. Then there's the Criminal Guilds, their powers are illegal as they all affect the Skinlands and the living. Rounding them is the Forbidden Guilds which are pretty hated in addition to illegal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted this categorisation comes from Wraith: the Great War, and Wr20 is tweaking some things about the Guilds (for instance, the Usurers were a Great Guild in W:tGW, but in Wr20 they have a bit more ambiguous standing, having a criminal faction).<br /> <br /> <br /> One of the major Arcanoi is a bit unusual when it comes to Arcanoi as wraithly skills - specifically, Pandemonium. Since the Haunters Guildbook, it originated with a pact with the Wyld, from Werewolf: The Apocalypse (well, the parts of the Wyld in the Dark Umbra), and seems to have become a natural wraith skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T07:55:49-08:00","id":340007,"title":"","content":"I never said the Arcanoi originate with the Guilds, I even point out that other Dark Kingdoms have the most of those Arcanoi themselves despite not having the Guilds or even contact with the Dark Kingdom of Iron. All the Arcanoi seem to some innate ability within wraiths, just unrefined. That's where the Guilds came in, they began to refine and develop those powers, in the process creating a monopoly over their particular Arcanoi as they were the first masters of these Arcanoi. The Breaking of the Guilds has undermined that power but still the greatest masters of the Arcanoi are those ancient wraiths of the Guilds.<br /> <br /> As for the Usurers, I'm not surprised. We never got a Guildbook for them and they are basically Pathos bankers so having a criminal faction within them does make sense. Hell I could see many wraiths viewing the Guild as greedy criminals that would screw over anyone and everyone for Pathos. But as much some wraiths complain about them, their powers are vital for the continued functioning of the Stygian society. That's why they're a Great Guild and not Working or Criminal one. People may not like them but they <i>need </i>them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T08:12:16-08:00","id":340044,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I think the guild metaphor is helpful for understanding them, insofar that Arcanoi are akin to the crafting skills of medieval European guilds, which also helps explain why there are both ancient and modern variations. Techniques and philosophies change over time. The arts of Castigate stick together both because of their logical grouping (powers that affect the Shadow) and because of the word of the Pardoners' Guild. It makes sense that other cultures would have developed arts related to affecting the Shadow (in the same way that other cultures would have developed carpentry), but their naming conventions and conceptual understanding of these arts would vary. In this model I guess the overarching categories exist more as a necessary gaming abstraction than as some kind of mystical glue within the world of Wraith, in the same way that any other World of Darkness monster isn't going to measure their strengths on a one-to-five scale just because that's how the information is presented to the players.<br /> <br /> Cool.<br /> <br /> I wonder why the authors chose the term &quot;Arcanos&quot; anyway? I guess because wraiths are normally invisible to mortals, and also because the ways and means of learning these arts are unintuitive to the recently deceased? If I were a newly-reaped wraith, and a Sandman were trying to explain Keening to me, I'd get learning how to play an instrument, but actually manipulating someone's emotions on a fundamental level would be at least a little bit alien, and require further explanation of concepts like Pathos.<br /> <br /> Actually, now that makes me wonder if all the Stygian Arcanoi can be &quot;mapped&quot; to some real-world art or craft, the sorts of things that would have been protected by medieval-style guilds.<br /> <br /> Keening: Music<br /> Moliate: Sculpture<br /> Usury: Finance<br /> Phantasm: Dramaturgy<br /> Castigate: Confession (Theology? Psychotherapy?)<br /> Inhabit: Smithing (Sort of? Artificers are weird, because their main thing seems to be Soulforging, but that's not an Arcanos, and the Inhabit part seems almost tacked on.)<br /> Puppetry: ...???<br /> <br /> Okay... I don't know where I'm going with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T09:52:16-08:00","id":340100,"title":"","content":"Exactly.<br /> <br /> As for Inhabit and the Artificers, they're a bit different from their peers as their Arcanoi isn't connected to what the Guild's most famous for. If you get the Artificers book they actually have a separate Soulforging skill. Speaking of the Guildbook, it actually has two separate variations on Inhabit, the Ancient Arts and the New Arts which involve computers and electronics. <br /> <br /> Though Inhabit can be used as a means to create relics by possessing an object in the Skinlands and having it destroyed.<br /> <br /> And while some Acranoi share traits with certain living professions or skills not all of them do. Some like Puppetry are pure ghostly things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T10:27:50-08:00","id":340118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi?p=340044#post340044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moliate: Sculpture</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if we're talking about what they Guild DOES, than the same way the Sandmen are a Guild of Actors, the Artificers are a Guild of smiths, the Usurers are a bank, the Pardoners are religious confessors, etc etc...<br /> <br /> The Masquers are an assassin guild primarily.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T10:30:06-08:00","id":340119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi?p=340100#post340100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly.<br /> <br /> As for Inhabit and the Artificers, they're a bit different from their peers as their Arcanoi isn't connected to what the Guild's most famous for. If you get the Artificers book they actually have a separate Soulforging skill</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed the Ancient Arts for Inhabit on the Kickstarter page bore much more directly to the role of smiths, which leads me to assume that the &quot;Ancient Arts&quot; are mainly going to be the Guild-only territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T10:46:26-08:00","id":340127,"title":"","content":"I'd say Guild only and older wraiths. In the New Arts of the Guildbook they have that any wraith who's been dead for more than 25 years must make a Willpower roll to see if they can grasp the concepts of modern electronics before they can learn the New Arts.<br /> <br /> I'd also probably homerule something along the lines of having a increased xp cost for younger wraiths in learning Anicent Arcanoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T11:00:12-08:00","id":340134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi?p=340127#post340127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Guild only and older wraiths. In the New Arts of the Guildbook they have that any wraith who's been dead for more than 25 years must make a Willpower roll to see if they can grasp the concepts of modern electronics before they can learn the New Arts.<br /> <br /> I'd also probably homerule something along the lines of having a increased xp cost for younger wraiths in learning Anicent Arcanoi.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just hope the Guilds have some actual proprietary secrets, rather than just reduced xp cost or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T11:06:07-08:00","id":340139,"title":"","content":"From the sound of things from the KS page, the Guilds will have a little bit more going on for them so yeah, probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T13:20:46-08:00","id":340187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi?p=340044#post340044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Puppetry: ...???<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Quite literally, Puppetry, as in the art of controlling puppets, or doll-making.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T13:31:21-08:00","id":340194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi?p=340118#post340118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Masquers are an assassin guild primarily.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not primarily, no. The guild does have an assassin (sort of) faction, but it's the beautician and armament sides that brings in most of the Oboli.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T06:40:14-08:00","id":340792,"title":"","content":"That's interesting.<br /> <br /> I'm going to hijack my own thread to ask another newbie-type question.<br /> <br /> Say you've decided to go out on a hike in the woods. You're out there by yourself for whatever reason. You're enjoying yourself, having a good time getting back to nature, when you run afoul of a water moccasin who is less than pleased at your almost trampling it.<br /> <br /> Next, you wake up in the Shadowlands. Before you know it, you've gotten a crash course on life after death, Stygia, Oblivion, and the Hierarchy. And, since you've got nothing better to do now, you decide to join up.<br /> <br /> Which Legion would this hypothetical you end up in? There doesn't seem to be one for &quot;death by nature,&quot; in the same way that there is the Threshold of the Prey in <i>Geist</i>. Does this fall under the Emerald Lord's purview? Is this an oversight on Charon's part? (That would be weird considering how long he's been around.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T06:47:14-08:00","id":340796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi?p=340792#post340792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interesting.<br /> <br /> I'm going to hijack my own thread to ask another newbie-type question.<br /> <br /> Say you've decided to go out on a hike in the woods. You're out there by yourself for whatever reason. You're enjoying yourself, having a good time getting back to nature, when you run afoul of a water moccasin who is less than pleased at your almost trampling it.<br /> <br /> Next, you wake up in the Shadowlands. Before you know it, you've gotten a crash course on life after death, Stygia, Oblivion, and the Hierarchy. And, since you've got nothing better to do now, you decide to join up.<br /> <br /> Which Legion would this hypothetical you end up in? There doesn't seem to be one for &quot;death by nature,&quot; in the same way that there is the Threshold of the Prey in <i>Geist</i>. Does this fall under the Emerald Lord's purview? Is this an oversight on Charon's part? (That would be weird considering how long he's been around.)</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Book of Legions, you'd fall under the Emerald Legion, which takes those who die from poison by animal bites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T10:05:11-08:00","id":340906,"title":"","content":"Coolio. Fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T10:41:29-08:00","id":340930,"title":"","content":"There might be a possibility for the Legion of Paupers, depending on how odd the water-moccasin encounter might have been and the details of who the person in question might have been - Maybe he had a weak blood vessel wall in his brain and had an embolism due to the shock of getting bit... so a split with the Skeletal Legion b/c of the prior existing disease... or ran off the edge of a ravine b/c he completely lost his shit over being bit, so there might be a Pentinent Legion claim for Madness... Or tried to save himself by the whole cut-the-wound-and- suck-out-the-poison thing (which is a very bad idea) but nicked an artery and, once he realized what he'd done, he just gave up and let himself go gently into that Iron Night, so a nod to the Silent Legion. If the cause of death was muddied by one or some of the above, the Beggar Lord's Reapers would definitely be trying to get ahold of his corpus....<br /> <br /> Or, like Eurydice, maybe his death by serpent was just meant to be and one of the Legion of Fate was waiting nearby to pull off his caul....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T11:24:06-08:00","id":341011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi?p=340930#post340930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or, like Eurydice, maybe his death by serpent was just meant to be and one of the Legion of Fate was waiting nearby to pull off his caul....</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">. . .and, instead of a snake-bite deathmark, there\u2019s an ouroboros where the wound should be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T11:43:45-08:00","id":341029,"title":"","content":"Yeah some times deaths don't neatly line up along Legion lines and it can be a source of conflict between them. Take American General George S. Patton who was severely injured in a car accident and then days later succumbed to his injuries. Some suggest the whole incident was unusual and even theorized that he was even assassinated for his loud, outspoken views against the Soviet Union. When he crossed over, both the Legion of Paupers and the Emerald Legion wanted him. The Fifth Great Maelstrom was going on and Stygia needed all the experienced soldiers it could get. A man like Patton was catch for any Legion and they were the only two that could by law claim him. Patton of course refused both Legions until he could learn exactly what it was he was getting himself into. Once he did learn all about Stygia, the Legions and Oblivion he joined up with the Paupers, serving today as a honorary Overload, traveling from Necropolis to Necropolis with a band of soldiers, lending whatever aid he can in the fight against Oblivion.<br /> <br /> And before someone asks me if that's real, it is. Take a look in the Hierarchy book, Patton's in the Legendary Hierarchs section.<br /> <br /> Of course Patton was lucky in that he got the choice, most wraiths of conflicted deaths don't. They get scooped up by whatever Legion that could fit their death finds them first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:38:47-08:00","id":341272,"title":"","content":"I now am convinced that in the years since the cancellation of WtO the Emerald Legion has gained the most renowned Doomslayer in centuries to its ranks...<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Aaaa crikey! Look at that mortwright there - he's a BUTE! I'm gonna wrassle 'em!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-15-2014, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value