code_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ATwannabe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi?p=342453#post342453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> aww, now I'm sad</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Because that crazy Aussie died doing what he loved?<br /> <br /> Don't be sad for him. Be thankful we had someone that nuts to show us the crazy world we lived in and know that, at least in the World of Darkness, he's continuing his work.<br /> <br /> &quot;Leviathan? Yeah, seen him before, he's a brute, but ya gotta love 'im!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T10:02:18-08:00","id":343061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi?p=340930#post340930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There might be a possibility for the Legion of Paupers, depending on how odd the water-moccasin encounter might have been and the details of who the person in question might have been - Maybe he had a weak blood vessel wall in his brain and had an embolism due to the shock of getting bit... so a split with the Skeletal Legion b/c of the prior existing disease...</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the Hierarchy reaping process involves long, boring, Kafka-esque judiciary intake hearings where they argue about things exactly like this, relying on a massive, labyrinthine case history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T12:38:00-08:00","id":343143,"title":"","content":"It's interesting that Stygia's categorization of deaths is very social, rather than, say, metaphysical. It reminds me of what Foucault was writing about in <i>The Order of Things</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T15:59:06-08:00","id":343405,"title":"","content":"What? You mean the creation of the Legions or how they were divided along death lines?<br /> <br /> Originally the Legions were actually, well like their name implies the protectors and soldiers of the original Stygian government which was a republic in the vein of the Roman Republic. It's not really clear on the nature of the original Legions, whether they were divided along death lines like they are in the modern day I can't say. Then the First Great Maelstrom hit the unsuspecting and unprepared Stygia. In the aftermath, Charon made a push to strengthen and militarize Stygia, replacing the Republic with the Empire of the modern age. Charon chose seven of the Senators were chosen as the first Deathlords and the Legions basically became the government.<br /> <br /> Though it does make me think, perhaps the original Legions where just military units and didn't necessarily have the death-nature division, sure there may have been units that were specifically home to a certain kind of death but most were just a collection of military minded wraiths. I could see the Senate being the one divided along death-lines, representing the wraiths who died along shared lines. And when Charon broke up the Republic and named the first Deathlords, choosing a Senator from each of seven main kinds of deaths with the Legion of Fate existing separately in some form or another and incorporated into the new regime.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T19:55:33-08:00","id":343592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bphillips</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/339568-what-are-arcanoi?p=343061#post343061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume the Hierarchy reaping process involves long, boring, Kafka-esque judiciary intake hearings where they argue about things exactly like this, relying on a massive, labyrinthine case history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm imagining it often happens as a fast and dirty first come first served event with Reapers grabbing who they can and ripping off cauls... Newly minted wraiths aren't really worth all that warngling. Definitely for someone famous who comes with heavy Memoriam from the get go. But your average wraith is probably just a snatch and grab, lucky to get the &quot;shackle 'em up&quot; nod instead of &quot;forge 'em down&quot;.<br /> <br /> I imagine a lot of cases might be easy to decide by looking at Deathmarks....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T20:26:42-08:00","id":343615,"title":"","content":"Definitely with the Legion of Fate. Few are willing to snatch up someone with the Deathmarks of Fate.<br /> <br /> But even with Deathmarks it doesn't always work out cleanly. During the early part of WWI there was a dispute between the Penitent and Silent Legions over those mentally broken by the war and killed themselves. On the one hand, they did kill themselves. On the other they were clearly suffering from madness of some form. So who do they go to? In the end it was declared they belonged to the Penitent Legion, not the Silent.<br /> <br /> Or what about a person who was murdered by someone suffering from a severe mental illness? Do they as a murder victim go to the Grim Legion? Or as victim of madness goes to the Penitent Legion? It's deaths like these that make things messy from the Hierarchy and one of the reasons why the Legions are always keeping an eye out for the newly dead, Better to snatch up those souls before those from other potential Legions can get them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T08:36:12-08:00","id":343914,"title":"","content":"There is definitely such wrangling going on, but the existence of Deathmarks would seem to make all that into thud and blunder. The corpus would always tell the truth... habeas nota morta?<br /> <br /> I can imagine with drones, if the Reaper can grab the wraith and get it to the soulforges, there might be some quibbling, but with any &quot;normal&quot; wraith, it would be hard to deny which Legion gets which wraith. They come pre-labelled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T10:42:08-08:00","id":343992,"title":"","content":"Indeed and most wraiths do bare the Deathmarks of only one Legion but like I said sometimes deaths don't always follow such clean lines. Like my earlier reference, George S. Patton's wraith was sought after by both the Paupers and the Emerald Legion, presumably because they both had recognized claim over him meaning his Deathmarks likely indicated that he could have belonged to either. Given the nature of his death and time leading up to it I can see that happening. After all the Paupers are very much the Legion of leftovers and people who's deaths don't quite fit with the other Legions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T12:19:20-08:00","id":344028,"title":"","content":"Are deathmarks only visible with Fatalism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T12:53:43-08:00","id":344036,"title":"","content":"No. Anyone can see Deathmarks and get an idea of how the person died, enough to make an educated guess at least. Fatalism allows a wraith to read and understand Deathmarks, allowing them to know the circumstances of a wraith's death and whatever additional meaning they have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T13:00:40-08:00","id":344040,"title":"","content":"I guess I need something more definitive about exactly what Deathmarks are and how they look. Is there individual variation or are they iconic? Can you have marks from more than one Legion?<br /> <br /> Can we SEE them in the art of the game? Maybe even get some temporary tattoos as a stretch goal? &gt;;-)<br /> <br /> Or Deathmark t-shirts with your Legion on the back? Or a Deathmark coffee cup? <br /> <br /> Deathmark/Legion shot glasses! Collect the whole set and drink like you are a Deathlord!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T14:54:17-08:00","id":344123,"title":"","content":"Well the way I see it Deathmarks, at least those involving <i>how</i> they died, reflecting the Legion character images in Wraith: the Great War.<br /> <br /> Which means that four of them can be more easily spotted.<br /> <br /> Skeletal Legion: gaunt and sickly, signs of the sickness that killed them<br /> <br /> Grim Legion: marks that represent their fatal wounds<br /> <br /> Iron Legion: physical apprentice aged to an exaggerated extent<br /> <br /> Emerald Legion: same as the Grim<br /> <br /> If you look at those four Legion characters from WtGW they all represent that to some form or another. The face of the Skeletal Legionnaire looks gaunt, with sunken cheeks. The Iron Legionnaire has cobwebs clinging to his body like some antique left in an attic to collect dust and cobwebs. The Grim man has visible bullet holes while the Emerald Legionnaire has been very clearly run over by a car.<br /> <br /> Added to this is the Legion of Fate who bare the marks of Fate in addition to whatever other signs of death they may have. Unfortunately WtGW doesn't really do good job in illustrating this as the image of the LoF is a pilot who's been virtually cut in two. However there is an earlier fluff bit in the book with a LoF member remembering his death and reaping by another LoF member, describing a symbol on his arm that sounds like the LoF symbol.<br /> <br /> The remaining three, Paupers, Penitent and Silent are a little harder to spot as they involve mystery, madness and despair. The Penitent of WtGW is a nurse with a number of stab wounds in her chest, implying that she worked at an asylum and was stabbed to death by a patient. The Silent is a particularly sad and pathetic looking soldier with no visible signs of how he killed himself. Finally the Pauper is a female factory worker, again no visible signs of what killed her though that might just be the point. Plus I know a bit about those times and what conditions in those factories were like back then and there are a number of things that could have killed her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T19:31:38-08:00","id":344317,"title":"","content":"And I always pictured them as actual MARKS not as in attributes of the wraith's corpus. The analogy to birthmarks and their description as &quot;traceries&quot; on the corpus made me think of lines, even rune-like lines. With appearance of the corpus was less a Deathmark than indicative of the wraith's self-image or quality time spent working with Moliate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T06:53:54-08:00","id":360182,"title":"","content":"I interpret Arcanoi as the development and refinement of different aspects of wraithly nature, and as such all of them are the expression of innate abilities of wraiths that can be mastered with enough trial and effort. They are not the proprietary knowledge of any Guild or Dark Kingdom, although to have link with the factions that have specialized in them can certainly make their development easier.<br /> <br /> I have strong objections to limiting Jade Arcanoi to Asian wraiths, for various reasons. There are various cases certain Stygian and Jade Arcanoi (e.g. the Castigate, Way of the Soul, and Way of the Farmer combo; the Keening, Intimate, and Way of the Scholar combo) synergize so well for their purposes that I expect the wraiths in Stygia and the Yellow Springs alike that really care for mastering fields like mental manipulation or Shadow/P'o control would strive to learn all of them. The Dark Kingdoms of Iron and Jade (and Western and East Asian civilizations) have been sharing contacts for a long time and with things like Pact of Doom and the Hive-Mind cultural barriers to exchange of knowledge do not matter that much for the dead anyway.<br /> <br /> Moreover and more importantly, since East Asian wraiths are told to know almost all Stygian Arcanoi, I assume it is only absolutely fair and necessary to give Stygian wraiths similar access to Jade Arcanoi and to suppose something similar to the global spread of Eastern martial arts took place. I care very little about political correctness issues and I'm proud of it but the notion of East Asian, African, or Indian wraiths having free access to Western or &quot;common&quot; mystical insights and being able to develop and hoard their own special arts rubs me seriously wrong in several ways.<br /> <br /> Last but not least, the Stygian and Yellow Springs notions of the soul seem so alike as to make the conclusion necessary the Psyche and Shadow, Hun and P'o, systems are petty much the same thing with different names and work the same way, and hence powers that target them are essentially compatible. Even Kuei-Jin basically seem a different type of Risen more than anything else. Therefore, I do not discern any serious metaphysical obstacles to a Stygian or Yellow Springs wraith mixing Stygian and Jade Arcanoi, not any more so than studying different Arcanoi in the first place. Chains of the Emperor, of course, may be a special exception and rather more difficult to learn for obvious reasons (lack of teachers). Things may or may not be different for other Dark Kingdoms arts, I have paid much less attention to Great War stuff, but probably they are not, since IIRC the two-part organization of the soul seems more or less universal for all modern Dark Kingdoms.<br /> <br /> Dark Arcanoi would not make much of a difference in this regard, apart from the fact I've more difficulty to understand why wraiths would be so interested in learning most Dark Arcanoi at all, although Doomslayers are told to be often so in their book. Most of them seem of exclusive use to Spectres or normal Arcanoi may do the same thing better for wraiths. The relevant exceptions seem Hive-Mind (it seems exceedingly useful for Doomslayers pulling espionage missions in the Labyrinth) and Larceny (any wraith may be potentially interested in a way to stave off Oblivion damage to Corpus). To a lesser degree, I could see a few Harbingers and Spooks of a martial bent being potentially interested in learning Tempestos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-05-2015, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}